 <year>1998</year>;<volume>4</volume>:<fpage>56</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>62</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10187067</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R5"><label>5. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Moran</surname><given-names>GJ</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Talan</surname><given-names>DA</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Mower</surname><given-names>W</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Newdow</surname><given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Ong</surname><given-names>S</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Nakase</surname><given-names>JY</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Appropriateness of rabies postexposure prophylaxis treatment for animal exposures.</article-title><source>JAMA</source>. <year>2000</year>;<volume>284</volume>:<fpage>1001</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.284.8.1001</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10944646</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R6"><label>6. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Tabel</surname><given-names>H</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Corner</surname><given-names>AH</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Webster</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Casey</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></string-name><article-title>History and epizootiology of rabies in Canada.</article-title><source>Can Vet J</source>. <year>1974</year>;<volume>15</volume>:<fpage>271</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>81</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">4608858</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R7"><label>7. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Rabies Research and Development Unit, Ontario Ministry of Natural Resources.</collab><article-title>Rabies in Ontario review of the year 2000.</article-title><source>The Rabies Reporter</source>. <year>2001</year>;<volume>11</volume>:<fpage>1</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>4</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R8"><label>8. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><string-name><surname>MacInnes</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>LeBer</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></string-name><article-title>Wildlife management agencies should participate in rabies control.</article-title><source>Wildl Soc Bull</source>. <year>2000</year>;<volume>28</volume>:<fpage>1156</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>67</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R9"><label>9. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="book"><collab>Ontario Ministry of Health</collab> 55th to 59th annual reports. Toronto: The Ministry; 1979/1980 to <year>1983/1984</year></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R10"><label>10. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Helmick</surname><given-names>CG</given-names></string-name><article-title>The epidemiology of human rabies postexposure prophylaxis, 1980-81.</article-title><source>JAMA</source>. <year>1983</year>;<volume>250</volume>:<fpage>1990</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1001/jama.250.15.1990</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6620498</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R11"><label>11. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><string-name><surname>MacInnes</surname><given-names>CD</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Tinline</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Ayers</surname><given-names>NR</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Bachmann</surname><given-names>P</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Ball</surname><given-names>DGA</given-names></string-name>, <etal/><article-title>Elimination of rabies from red foxes in eastern Ontario.</article-title><source>J Wildl Dis</source>. <year>2001</year>;<volume>37</volume>:<fpage>119</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>32</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11272485</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R12"><label>12. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Public Health Branch, Ontario Ministry of Health.</collab><article-title>Rabies post-exposure treatment (PET): Ontario, April 1 to June 30, 1998.</article-title><source>Public Health and Epidemiology Report Ontario</source>. <year>1999</year>;<volume>10</volume>:<fpage>16</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>8</lpage></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R13"><label>13. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><string-name><surname>Rupprecht</surname><given-names>CE</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Smith</surname><given-names>JS</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Fekadu</surname><given-names>M</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Childs</surname><given-names>JE</given-names></string-name><article-title>The ascension of wildlife rabies: a cause of public health concern or intervention?</article-title><source>Emerg Infect Dis</source>. <year>1995</year>;<volume>1</volume>:<fpage>107</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8903179</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R14"><label>14. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="confproc"><string-name><surname>Mitchell</surname><given-names>KD</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Heilman</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Howard</surname><given-names>BW</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Agnew</surname><given-names>EW</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></string-name> Raccoon rabies&#x02014;the urban challenge [abstract]. Proceedings of the 10th Annual International Meeting of Rabies in the Americas, San Diego, California, <year>1999</year> San Diego: California Association of Public Health Directors; 1999. p. 90</mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R15"><label>15. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention</collab><article-title>Human rabies&#x02014;Connecticut, 1995.</article-title><source>MMWR Morb Mortal Wkly Rep</source>. <year>1996</year>;<volume>45</volume>:<fpage>207</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8609874</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R16"><label>16. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Population and Public Health Branch</collab><article-title>Health Canada. A case report&#x02014;human rabies in Montreal, Quebec&#x02014;October, 2000.</article-title><source>Can Commun Dis Rep</source>. <year>2000</year>;<volume>26</volume>:<fpage>209</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>10</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11211598</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R17"><label>17. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><string-name><surname>McWilliam</surname><given-names>RS</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Penistan</surname><given-names>JL</given-names></string-name><article-title>Immunization against rabies.</article-title><source>Can Med Assoc J</source>. <year>1967</year>;<volume>94</volume>:<fpage>153</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6066820</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R18"><label>18. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><collab>Rabies Immunization</collab> Revised Regulations of Ontario. <article-title>Reg. 567. Amended to O.</article-title><source>Reg</source>. <year>1990</year>;<volume>331</volume></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="R19"><label>19. </label><mixed-citation publication-type="confproc"><string-name><surname>Voigt</surname><given-names>D</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Tinline</surname><given-names>RR</given-names></string-name> Fox rabies and trapping: a study of disease and fur harvest interaction. In: Sanderson GG, editor. Midwest furbearer management: proceedings of the symposium held at the 43rd Midwest Wildlife Conference. Washington: The Wildlife Society;<year>1982</year> p. 139-56.</mixed-citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>